{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1262a776ef0c77b153bafac67d8249c28b942f2128b61836a753178b3926eaa2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"2389-research/fleet-control@efe2657f5465 snapshot e6a4a546b9278950","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b0d886148b1553eab3182868546ac844fafcc94fc2aaa936a236d817b4dba056"],"source_ids":["src_4b8c3616b6125cb48740031cc4bde733"],"text":"Core principles include observer-not-launcher, zero agent instrumentation, CLI/MCP parity over one internal API, a single binary, CGO-free builds, and no elevated privileges.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3b00d59dec249dcc84975206f9165510ac33cda8d07f33be14aee427cd893989","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"2389-research/fleet-control@efe2657f5465 snapshot e6a4a546b9278950","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_009517e77b0277f6f5f02dd933d9fc4b53bb9e3d059fecd52320073fc14982ba"],"source_ids":["src_4b8c3616b6125cb48740031cc4bde733"],"text":"The design spec describes a Go binary `control` that observes and manages running AI agents via tmux introspection, offering visibility, stopping, and session history.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_41d50af997e98ff064758c1d6a60c61f9e57430e1958486ce41f324ae5be1272","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"2389-research/fleet-control@efe2657f5465 snapshot e6a4a546b9278950","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_670ec33a2c19e588761e28fe3bcaacb94c5d8c817e0a8d921f3a09e4b7255914","slc_6e45d1518da96d8fe6afe96e025ba5bac1d960aa602bf68dce3f2f2180e109a1","slc_b52ee7349df09a84c7835d294c16eef9c4bea2e7cc0856a39e573757f7328261"],"source_ids":["src_4b8c3616b6125cb48740031cc4bde733","src_7c9d9d6141c75b87bda40a5e4a3c0b46"],"text":"The architecture has three layers in one Go module: a `controld` daemon, a `control` CLI, and an MCP server, with the CLI and MCP as thin clients over the daemon's HTTP API.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4710e0ea7da04c5390633f588e7967aaccdd469c76f085280b214dc5504121ef","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"2389-research/fleet-control@efe2657f5465 snapshot e6a4a546b9278950","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_436fd81df8714241b532920670a499904c0e8d2c9558a4925650842955d51c96","slc_440bd5fd662ab17f7d4f9a593abe9daabad3089af0e189ddf7e42b49a46fc8c7"],"source_ids":["src_4b8c3616b6125cb48740031cc4bde733"],"text":"A redaction pass strips secret patterns (API keys, KEY/SECRET/TOKEN/PASSWORD env assignments, connection strings) before storage, replacing them with [REDACTED]; raw scrollback is never persisted or served.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5b02b3aca20bfd8d5a546d4345363a8e83da9a8d4a039fa55e1fa6e19b7f176a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"2389-research/fleet-control@efe2657f5465 snapshot e6a4a546b9278950","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b2a78389aa2741d44c727d91938eab340b1c45c253eb81b956c692151f7fe463"],"source_ids":["src_4b8c3616b6125cb48740031cc4bde733"],"text":"Stopping an agent resolves the pane's process tree, verifies PID identity, then escalates SIGINT to SIGTERM after 5s and optionally SIGKILL with --force, exiting code 4 on failure.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6310a43d48c89d8978f5d98b9625d09a4daa97fb66d62eb5f22d01c437b9156d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"2389-research/fleet-control@efe2657f5465 snapshot e6a4a546b9278950","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6f679ddb9b41ce5202ae62be62fe9a91e197b01ad708ebc564558b47ad793332","slc_c596e1bf165aad61e64404d540a38b053b232f07c60393f3ac72a4fca45b9498","slc_ceaa6ec5a5cefc41f87c35e9d35801dea50f00aa754fa57de81479795d087907"],"source_ids":["src_4b8c3616b6125cb48740031cc4bde733"],"text":"Socket security relies on file permissions (0700 directory, 0600 socket/db/pid); the trust boundary is same-user access, and socket paths over 104 bytes fall back to /tmp/control-<uid>.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6fcf964319deb6a492a20b2b5b40d61e8b627802d76876554abcc0a3e6b2f746","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"2389-research/fleet-control@efe2657f5465 snapshot e6a4a546b9278950","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b6191241085a1a60a2e9e0b4ea4f707ffdd59fe69b8cfb59f7b1ad148b0464a","slc_3892c0ba7a17fbcefbc149dcb39cfe2560ba25f356f2b65482b716f07a5c951f","slc_85adb8b85cd611c4b65ad8e93adc4a0ab30754ff2a7baa64943e8fcc79698d75"],"source_ids":["src_4b8c3616b6125cb48740031cc4bde733"],"text":"Live state is held in memory under an RWMutex with per-agent fields such as pane ID, type, PID, process start time, and a scrollback high-water mark; only parsed summaries are kept, not raw scrollback.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:26:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bf831e37322444acbb9eba8a72244a10"}
